s well so wild-type  animals are here and heterozygous  animals have much higher power  especially in this kind of low frequency  Delta band and here's looking at average  Delta power between wild-type and  heterozygous animals you can see that  significantly increased so in  collaboration with AstraZeneca we were  also able to test some novel compounds  to see if we could normalize some of the  consequences of a is synapse dysfunction  and so we had a look at these novel  selective benzodiazepines and these are  benzodiazepine compounds so they bind to  the benzodiazepine site but they're  specific either for alpha 2 or alpha 1 3  and so we tested a compound called AZ d7  3 to 5 that's an alpha 2 selective  benzodiazepine like drug or positive  allosteric modulator and again here  we're looking at the elevated plus maze  paradigm and what we can see is that we  have vehicle treated diazepam treated  and azd treated animals here and we're  comparing wild-type in white to  heterozygous animals in gray and again  replicating our prior data we can see  that heterozygous animals treated with  vehicle are much more anxious than their  wild-type counterparts and interestingly  when we treat with diazepam we can see a  decrease in anxiety in the wild-type  mice but the anxiety in the GABA to one  mice didn't seem to change however both  groups showed a decrease in anxiety when  treated with the azd compound is 87 3 to  5 and here in this graph we're just  looking at heterozygous animals and  comparing the 3 groups in terms of their  percent close time and we can see  vehicle and diazepam treated  heterozygous animals are spending you  know close to 90 percent of their time  or yeah 90 percent of their time in the  closed arms and in comparison when we  treat them with a zd7 3 to 5 we see a  significant reduction we also pursued  testing some of these selective  benzodiazepines for normalizing the EEG  as well and so here again we have  baseline recordings from wild-type and  heterozygous mice and the red line here  represents our administration of ACD 7 3  to 5 and so what we can see is that  shortly after administration of azd  compound we see this powerful reduction  in Delta activity that's relatively long  costing and even though it still has a  little more power overall in this  example in comparison to wild-type  this was a significant reduction in  Delta power we can see that plotted over  here so this is fast Fourier transform  analysis again we're looking at  normalized power and frequency on this  axis so this is the Delta frequencies  and up top here we can see these are  heterozygous animals at baseline and  when treated with the azd compound they  move down and largely overlap with the  wild-type frequencies and here we're  looking at theta frequency because we  can also see some alterations in theta  as well with a ZD compound and so here  we've got heterozygous baseline and then  we can see that suppression of theta by  the ACD compound over to summarize some  of the research that we've talked about  so far the gaba-a receptor alpha 2  subunit we've shown as a preferential  interacting partner with kali biston and  this is again kind of a new finding  because we thought that Jevon was a  partner for all of the alpha 1 through 3  subunits so once we were able to  identify that kali biston was a unique  interacting partner of this portion of  alpha 2 then we decided to mutate it and  so mutation of alpha amino acids 358  through 375 of the alpha 2 subunit of  the gaba-a receptor  results in increased expression of the  alpha 2 subunit but it is miss localized  and it doesn't reach the axon initial  segment and we also see a corresponding  loss of inhibitory synapses there and so  this suggests that even though other  subunits can get to the axon initial  segment they're not sufficient to help  wire wire it up properly from the  chandelier cells so when alpha 2 can't  get there we end up losing those  inhibitory synapses 